<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grutte Pier</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1480–<a href="/years/1520">1520</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Pier Gerlofs Donia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Grutte Pier (Pier Gerlofs Donia) was a Frisian farmer and rebel leader, famed for his size and strength. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> troops burned his village of Kimswerd in 1515, he waged a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war against the Saxon and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> rulers of Friesland with the support of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-ii-duke-of-guelders">Charles of Egmond</a>, Duke of Guelders, and his ships raided the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zuiderzee">Zuiderzee</a> coast of Holland. He gave up the leadership in 1519 and died in 1520.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/grutte-pier.jpg" alt="Grutte Pier" width="320" height="560" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pieter Feddes van Harlingen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grutte_Pier_(Pier_Gerlofs_Donia),_1622,_book_illustration.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
